title: Authorizations › Sites › Reviews, step-down plans and ledger cases at each site
route: /authorizations?view=reviews
intro: What Case Manager's site rules became. Every tracked case, review and accepted denial belongs to one site, the same site on every screen. The Approved and Reviews this week views, the review buttons, the bulk review actions, the step-down rows, the tracked quick view and the ledger case page all follow the site view. A viewer limited to one site never sees, counts, drafts or signs the other site's cases, and a direct link to one shows an out-of-site card.
dir: TD
also: Demo only, Both sites at the start: Approved 32 = Site A 17 + Site B 15; Reviews this week 47 = 26 + 21. Case Manager's own sidebar bubble is gone; the Authorizations badge follows the site the same way (19 = 11 + 8).
---
start s1 "Switch the site in the top bar: Both sites, Site A or Site B\nOr Demo menu › 'Viewing as': Dr. Rivera (Site A only), Sam Okafor (Site B only)"
goto gW "Continues in: Authorizations › Worklist › Sites: what each viewer sees"
screen sc1 "The tracked rows follow the view\nApproved and Reviews this week chips, their rows and their deadline counts\nA small 'Site A' tag after the title when the view is narrowed"
process p1 "Both sites = Site A + Site B for every count\nApproved 32 = 17 + 15, Reviews this week 47 = 26 + 21"
decision d1 "Is the viewer limited to one site?"
process p3 "The other site's cases do not exist for the viewer: not listed, not found by the search, not counted"
process p4 "A viewer of both sites narrows to one site and widens again; every number changes at once"
process p5 "'Draft all due reviews' and 'Sign all clean drafts' act only on reviews at the sites in view\nThe toast counts only those"
goto g3 "Continues in: Authorizations › Reviews this week › Draft all due reviews and sign all clean drafts"
process p6 "An accepted denial's step-down row is shown at the denial's own site"
process p7 "A ?quick= or ?review= for the other site's case opens nothing\nAn open quick view closes when its case leaves the view"

start s2 "Open a link to a case\n/authorizations/case/ID from a row, a review's 'Open case', a notification or a bookmark"
decision d2 "Is the case at a site in view?"
screen ok "The case page opens as usual\n(Authorizations case page, or the ledger case page)"
goto g4 "Continues in: Authorizations › Ledger case page › Open and read"
screen o1 "Out-of-site card instead of the page\n'This case is not available at Site A'\n'R-0856 belongs to Site B ...' with no patient or detail"
decision d3 "Can the viewer see both sites?"
click c1 "Click 'Show Site B'"
process p8 "The view widens to that site and the case opens"
click c2 "Click 'Back to the Dashboard'"
goto g1 "Continues in: Dashboard › Arrive › What the page shows"
endx e1 "A viewer limited to one site has no way to the other site's case"
goto g2 "Continues in: Authorizations › Case page › A case at another site"

s1 --> sc1 --> p1
s1 -.-> gW
sc1 --> d1
d1 -->|Yes| p3
d1 -->|No| p4
sc1 -.-> p5 --> g3
sc1 -.-> p6
sc1 -.-> p7
s2 --> d2
d2 -->|Yes| ok
ok -.-> g4
d2 -->|No| o1 --> d3
d3 -->|Yes| c1 --> p8 --> ok
d3 -->|No| e1
o1 --> c2 --> g1
o1 -.-> g2
